SuperMgmt: manage your infrastructure

Usage:
  sm [flags]
  sm [command]

Available Commands:
  approvals   List jobs awaiting approval with the plan hash to approve against
  completion  Generate a shell completion script
  config      Inspect and validate configuration
  docker      Open lazydocker on a node over SSH
  doctor      Diagnose configuration, paths and database health
  events      List audit events
  help        Help about any command
  jobs        List and govern jobs (default: list)
  nodes       List, add, inspect and probe nodes
  services    List services, read their logs and start, stop or restart them
  ssh         Open an interactive shell on a node with your own SSH credentials
  ssh-key     Show the instance SSH identity
  status      Show the daemon identity, node reachability and pending work
  version     Print version, commit, build date, Go version and platform

Flags:
      --config string      path to the configuration file
  -h, --help               help for sm
      --json               machine-readable JSON output
      --log-level string   log level: debug|info|warn|error (default "info")

Use "sm [command] --help" for more information about a command.

The TUI arrives in milestone M1; see ROADMAP.md.
